---
description: Which vps-setup-one-shot runbook to read when the user wants to set up, check, fix, upgrade, rebuild, stage or hand over their Coolify server or an app on it.
alwaysApply: false
---
The markdown is the source; nothing here repeats it. Work from the repo root, read the file, follow it exactly, in the user's language.

- A server from nothing (Hetzner or any Ubuntu 24.04 box, Coolify, the starter app): `SETUP.md`
- One-screen health, read-only: run `status.sh`; fixes are in `DOCTOR.md`
- The app is down, a deploy failed, 502 or a certificate error: `DOCTOR.md`
- The monthly checkup: `CHECKUP.md`
- An existing app onto the server, from the app's own repo: `PREPARE-APP.md`
- A staging copy of an app (staging branch, own database, staging domain), promotion by merge: `STAGING.md`
- Back to the previous version after a bad deploy: `ROLLBACK.md`
- A database back from an off-site backup: `RESTORE.md`
- A self-hosted tool on its own domain (Umami, n8n, Uptime Kuma, Forgejo): `SERVICES.md`
- Uptime checks for the apps and a public status page (Uptime Kuma): `UPTIME.md`
- Coolify, Ubuntu or Postgres major upgrades: `UPGRADE.md`
- A new server from nothing with the databases from the backups: `REBUILD.md`
- A server or project to a client, a colleague joining, old access removed: `HANDOVER.md`
